---
import { ArrowRight, GitPullRequest } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BadgePanel from '../components/BadgePanel.astro';
import { communityLinks } from '../lib/community';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contributing" description="Share a Power Platform snippet, help another maker, and get started with Sharing is Caring.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Your shortcut could be someone else's breakthrough" title="Small contribution. Real impact." description="A useful formula, a thoughtful component, or a helpful agent topic. You don't need a whole solution to share something valuable." portrait={2}><a class="button button--primary" href="https://github.com/pnp/powerplatform-snippets/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"><GitPullRequest size={17} /> Read the contribution guide</a></PageHero>
  <div class="container section-space"><BadgePanel actionHref="#contribution-steps" actionLabel="See how to contribute" /></div>
  <section class="content-section content-section--soft" id="contribution-steps"><ol class="container steps-grid">
    <li><h2>Find its home.</h2><p>Check for a similar snippet first. Fork the repository, create a branch, and choose the matching product category. Sign the Microsoft Contributor License Agreement.</p></li>
    <li><h2>Make it reusable.</h2><p>Use the category's README template. Include the snippet, setup instructions, prerequisites, a real screenshot, and complete assets/sample.json metadata with your author details.</p></li>
    <li><h2>Validate and share.</h2><p>Build the gallery locally, check your preview and documentation, then open a focused pull request. Share what you tested and anything the next maker needs to know.</p></li>
  </ol></section>
  <section class="container content-section two-columns">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Keep it focused</p><h2>A little structure helps.</h2><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Snippet folder structure"><code>{`power-apps/your-snippet-name/
  README.md
  assets/
    sample.json
    preview.png
  ...snippet source files`}</code></pre><p>Choose <code>copilot-studio</code>, <code>power-apps</code>, <code>power-automate-desktop</code>, or <code>power-pages</code>. Use lowercase folder names without dots and follow the product-specific naming guidance.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/pnp/powerplatform-snippets/tree/main/templates">Choose a README template <ArrowRight size={16} /></a></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Help someone try it</p><h2>Show the working result.</h2><ul><li>Give your snippet an accurate name, summary, products, categories, dates, and author information.</li><li>Store a screenshot in its own assets folder and reference it in both the README and metadata. Include useful alternative text.</li><li>Explain configuration, permissions, connectors, licensing, and any experimental requirements.</li><li>Use canonical main-branch source URLs and retain one correctly keyed tracking image as the final README line.</li></ul><p>Don't include secrets, credentials, private data, or production data in source files or screenshots.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container content-section content-narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Sharing is caring</p><h2>You don't have to do it alone.</h2><p>Our <a href={communityLinks.sharingIsCaring}>Sharing is Caring sessions</a> provide hands-on guidance for first-time contributors. Start with a documentation improvement or share the small pattern that helped you.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Gallery validation commands"><code>{`cd site
npm ci
npm run validate:readme-trackers
npm test
npm run check
npm run build
npm run validate:links`}</code></pre><p>For gallery interface changes, also run <code>npm run test:e2e</code>. The generator reports incomplete snippets rather than hiding them.</p><p>Replace the category and folder name below with your snippet's exact repository path:</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Snippet view tracking image"><code>{`<img src="https://m365-visitor-stats.azurewebsites.net/powerplatform-snippets/power-apps/your-snippet-name" />`}</code></pre></section>
</BaseLayout>
